.TH KCHANGELOG 1 "May 2026" "kchangelog 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kchangelog \- monitor Ubuntu kernel changelogs with desktop notifications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kchangelog
[\fIversion\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B kchangelog
.B \-\-subscribe
.I version
.br
.B kchangelog
.B \-\-unsubscribe
.I version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kchangelog
downloads and monitors Ubuntu kernel changelogs directly from Ubuntu servers. It helps users track security fixes (CVEs) and new package version releases. It can run interactively in the terminal or persistently via a background systemd user timer.
.PP
If no kernel version is specified, it defaults to the active running kernel version (obtained via `uname -r`).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Query Options
.TP
.BI \-\-cve
Filter the changelog output to show only sections that contain CVE identifiers.
.TP
.BI \-\-last " N"
Limit the output to the last \fIN\fR changelog entries.
.TP
.BI \-\-diff
Compare the downloaded changelog against the last saved baseline version in \fI~/.config/kchangelog/seen/\fR. Offers to update the baseline.
.TP
.BI \-\-open
Pipe the changelog output into the system pager (defaults to \fIless \-R\fR).
.TP
.BI \-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\-available
Retrieve and list all available kernel package versions found in the local APT cache.
.TP
.BI \-\-grep " pattern"
Filter changelog entry blocks by matching a keyword pattern (case-insensitive).
.TP
.BI \-\-json
Format the changelog output as a structured JSON array of objects.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Specify when to apply ANSI terminal colors to output (defaults to \fBauto\fR, which colorizes only when outputting directly to an interactive terminal TTY).
.SS Subscription Options
.TP
.BI \-\-subscribe " version"
Subscribe to background changelog monitoring for a specific kernel version or \fBactive\fR to track the running kernel.
.TP
.BI \-\-unsubscribe " version"
Unsubscribe from background monitoring for a specific kernel version.
.TP
.BI \-\-list\-subs
List all current active subscriptions.
.SS Service & Admin Options
.TP
.BI \-\-check
Check all active subscriptions now (used by the background systemd timer).
.TP
.BI \-\-install\-service
Install and register the systemd user service and timer for background periodic checking (runs every 6 hours).
.TP
.BI \-\-remove\-service
Uninstall and clean up the systemd user service and timer.
.TP
.BI \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display the help menu and exit.
.TP
.BI \-v\fR, \fB\-\-version
Display version and copyright information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kchangelog/subscriptions
A plain text file containing one kernel version string per line representing the active subscriptions.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kchangelog/seen/
Directory containing baseline changelog files used for diff comparisons.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/kchangelog.service
The systemd user service unit.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/kchangelog.timer
The systemd user timer unit running every 6 hours.
.SH EXAMPLES
Query the changelog for the active kernel:
.IP
.B kchangelog
.PP
Show only CVE entries in the last 3 releases of kernel 6.8:
.IP
.B kchangelog 6.8 --cve --last 3
.PP
Subscribe to the active kernel:
.IP
.B kchangelog --subscribe active
.PP
List all available kernels for monitoring:
.IP
.B kchangelog --list-available
